        "text": "Skip to content\n# Roemerwise\nRoemers helping Orinda prevent fire\n# Home\n## Practical wildfire preparedness for Lamorinda homes\nI’m Mike Roemer — an Orinda resident, MOFD Board Director for Division 4, and Firewise Ambassador. This site collects the low-cost, high-impact steps that make East Bay hills homes far more likely to survive an ember storm, along with fire-science research and news from the Moraga-Orinda Fire District.\nStart here: harden your home\nReelection 2026\n### Three things you can do this weekend\n#### Screen your vents\nInstall 1/16-inch steel mesh over foundation and attic vents so embers can’t ignite your crawl space or insulation. How to do it →\n#### Cover soffit holes\nFirebrands enter through small openings under your eaves. Covering soffit holes with steel mesh takes an afternoon. Watch the video →\n#### Clear the first five feet\nThe zone closest to your walls matters most. Replace bark mulch with gravel, and keep combustibles away from siding and eaves during fire season.\n#### Latest posts\nAugust 10, 2026\nMy November 2022 article in The Orinda News on the fire-flood connection: atmospheric rivers, debris flows on burn scars, and evacuation planning for single-exit roads.\nAugust 10, 2026\nSpokane residents watched their homes burn through their doorbell cameras. The WSJ’s account — and why it’s the strongest case yet for the 5-foot Zone Zero.\nJuly 29, 2026\nCanyon’s practice evacuation drew about 80 residents — a model for every Lamorinda neighborhood. Lamorinda Weekly’s coverage, with my thoughts from the drill.\nJuly 22, 2026\nA piece I wrote for The Orinda News on how a warming atmosphere holds more water vapor, why that turns Lamorinda creeks into debris-flow hazards, and what “go-bag” readiness means…\nJuly 17, 2026\nThe Five Foot Zone Zero (5Z0), the name for the five feet immediately adjacent from the entire perimeter of your home, is one of the most effective areas for defending…\nSee all posts →\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nRoemerwise\nHave a WordPress.com account? Log in now.\nRoemerwise\nCopy shortlink\nView post in Reader\nManage subscriptionsSign upLog in\nReport this content\nCollapse this bar",
